  "hints": [
    "Checking every later element is O(n^2). Think about which elements are still 'waiting' for a bigger value.",
    "Keep a stack of indices whose answer is not yet known. When a[i] arrives, it is the answer for every waiting index with a smaller value.",
    "Those waiting indices have non-increasing values from bottom to top, so the ones a[i] beats sit on top of the stack: pop while a[top] < a[i], set their answer to i, then push i."
  ],
  "editorial": "Maintain a stack of indices whose next greater element has not been found. Invariant: the values on the stack are **non-increasing** from bottom to top (if a new value were larger than the top it would have popped it). When `a[i]` arrives, every waiting index with a smaller value finds its answer at `i`; they are exactly the top run of the stack, so we pop while `a[top] < a[i]`, record `i`, then push `i`. Equal values are not popped because the comparison is strict.\n\nEach index is pushed and popped at most once: `O(n)` total.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n# next strictly greater index for each position\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// next strictly greater index for each position\n// readLine() returns the next input line (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    // next strictly greater index for each position\n    return 0;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        // next strictly greater index for each position\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1+n]))\nres = [0] * n\nst = []\nfor i in range(n):\n    while st and a[st[-1]] < a[i]:\n        res[st.pop()] = i + 1\n    st.append(i)\nprint(' '.join(map(str, res)))\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst res = new Array(n).fill(0);\nconst st = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n  while (st.length && a[st[st.length - 1]] < a[i]) res[st.pop()] = i + 1;\n  st.push(i);\n}\nconsole.log(res.join(' '));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StreamTokenizer in = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        in.nextToken();\n        int n = (int) in.nval;\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { in.nextToken(); a[i] = (long) in.nval; }\n        int[] res = new int[n];\n        int[] st = new int[n];\n        int top = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            while (top > 0 && a[st[top - 1]] < a[i]) res[st[--top]] = i + 1;\n            st[top++] = i;\n        }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { if (i > 0) sb.append(' '); sb.append(res[i]); }\n        System.out.println(sb);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    vector<int> res(n, 0), st;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        while (!st.empty() && a[st.back()] < a[i]) {\n            res[st.back()] = i + 1;\n            st.pop_back();\n        }\n        st.push_back(i);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cout << res[i] << (i + 1 < n ? ' ' : '\\n');\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  }
